hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"16813","Abd Allah narrated to us, he said: Surayj ibn Yunus narrated to me from his book, he said: Abbad ibn Abbad, meaning al-Muhallabi, narrated to us from Abd Allah ibn Uthman ibn Khuthaym from Sa'id ibn Abi Rashid, a freedman of the family of Mu'awiya, he said: I came to Syria, and it was said to me: In this church is the messenger of Caesar to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: So we entered the church, and there I was with an old man, and I said to him: Are you the messenger of Caesar to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? And he said: Yes. He said: I said: Narrate to me about that. He said: When he campaigned to Tabuk, he wrote a letter to Caesar and sent it with a man called Dihya ibn Khalifa, and when he read his letter he placed it with him upon his couch, and he sent for his commanders and the chiefs of his companions and said: This man has sent a messenger to you and written you a letter giving you a choice of one of three: either you follow him upon his religion, or you acknowledge to him a tribute running for him upon you while he leaves you upon your condition in your lands, or you cast war to him. He said: And they snorted a snort until some of them came out of their hooded cloaks, and they said: We will not follow him upon his religion and leave our religion and the religion of our fathers, nor acknowledge to him a tribute running for him upon us, but we will cast war to him. And he said: That had been so, but I disliked deciding a matter without you. Abbad said: And I said to Ibn Khuthaym: Had he not drawn near and intended Islam, as has reached us? He said: Yes, were it not that he saw from them. He said: And he said: Seek for me a man from the Arabs with whom I may write to him the answer to his letter. He said: And I came, while I was a young man, and I was taken to him, and he wrote his answer and said to me: Whatever you forget of anything, retain from me three traits: See, when he reads my letter, whether he mentions the night and the day, and whether he mentions his letter to me, and see whether you see upon his back a mark. He said: So I came until I reached him while he was at Tabuk in a circle of his companions sitting with their legs drawn up, and I asked and was told about him, and I handed him the letter, and he called Mu'awiya and he read the letter to him, and when he came to his saying: You invited me to a Paradise whose expanse is the heavens and the earth, so where is the Fire? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the night comes, where is the day? He said: And he said: I wrote to al-Najashi and he tore it, so Allah tore his kingdom in shreds, the torn of kingdom. Abbad said: And I said to Ibn Khuthaym: Did not al-Najashi accept Islam, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) announce his death in Medina to his companions and pray over him? He said: Yes, that was so-and-so son of so-and-so, and this is so-and-so son of so-and-so; Ibn Khuthaym mentioned them all and I forgot them. And I wrote to Khosrau a letter and he tore it, so Allah tore his kingdom in shreds, and I wrote to Caesar a letter and he answered me in it, and the people never ceased fearing some might from them as long as there was good in life. Then he said to me: Who are you? I said: From Tanukh. He said: O brother of Tanukh, do you have any desire for Islam? I said: No, I came from among a people and I am among them upon a religion, and I will not exchange their religion until I return to them. He said: And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) laughed, or smiled. And when I had fulfilled my need I stood, and when I turned he called me and said: O brother of Tanukh, come, proceed with what you were commanded. He said: And I had forgotten them, and I turned from behind the circle, and he cast aside a cloak that was upon him from his back, and I saw the cartilage of his shoulder like the large cupping mark."
"16814","Abd Allah narrated to us, he said: Abu Amir Hawthara ibn Ashras narrated to me from dictation to me, he said: Hammad ibn Salama informed me from Abd Allah ibn Uthman ibn Khuthaym from Sa'id ibn Abi Rashid, he said: The messenger of Caesar was a neighbor of mine in the time of Yazid ibn Mu'awiya, and I said to him: Inform me about the letter of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to Caesar. And he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent Dihya al-Kalbi to Caesar and wrote with him to him a letter, and he mentioned the like of the hadith of Abbad ibn Abbad, and the hadith of Abbad is more complete and better in relating the hadith, and he added: He said: And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) laughed when he invited him to Islam and he refused to accept Islam, and he recited this verse: You do not guide whom you love, but Allah guides whom He wills. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You are the messenger of a people, and you have a right, but you came to us while we are destitute. And Uthman ibn Affan said: I will clothe him with a yellowish garment, and a man from the Ansar said: His hospitality is upon me."
